Based on the upstream V2-era code structure (Chrome extension, vanilla JS +
jQuery/lodash + compiled templates). The upstream project has since evolved
separately to V3.0 (Manifest V3, WXT + TypeScript + Vue3); the two codebases
are no longer the same code and do not depend on each other. Archived source
of our extension-era code lives on the `extension` branch and the
`archive/extension-v4.8.0` tag of this repository, kept for reference only.

Major modifications compared to the upstream V2 baseline (summary):
  - Windows desktop application (Electron) wrapping the collection engine as
    `desktop/src/engine`, with a Vue 3 renderer, task state machine,
    resumable download manager, and per-task checkpoint persistence
  - Prebuilt offline archive viewer bundled at
    `desktop/src/engine/export-resources/spa-dist/`
  - Retrieval-layer split (api/collectors/repos/exporters/packagers/tasks),
    IPC contract hardening (source guard, channel whitelist), structured
    dual-track logging, and removal of the experimental deleted-messages
    recovery feature (v4.9)

This product relies on QQ Zone's internal web APIs; it is for personal
backup of your own data only. Use at your own risk.
